Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 20:46:32 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] fix(ui): keep the offline banner out of the status bar

The app draws edge to edge (target SDK 36: Android 15 and later enforce
it), and the offline banner sat above the stack with no top inset: on
those phones it was drawn under the status bar, over the clock, and
Maestro's 05-offline could not see it there.

OfflineBanner now takes the status bar's place (the top inset as its
padding) and wraps the screens below it, which get a top inset of 0
while it shows, so their headers do not leave that space a second time.
The tree below stays the same online and offline: the navigation state
is kept. A component spec covers the insets and the single mount; the
05-offline flow passes on an API 36 emulator.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
